// A lambda's parameters are declarations, so §4.1 reaches them: nothing
// shadows anything. This is the cost the design charges where it is most
// annoying -- short parameter names in a function with short locals -- and
// the fix is the rename the rule always asks for.
interface Get { int of(int k); }
int n = 3;
Get g = (int n) => n;
print(g.of(1));
